  "overview": "**Digital NSW** is a light-first design system anchored on `#fff` canvas surfaces with `#0b0b0c` primary ink (19.7:1 contrast) and `#002664` brand accent.\n\nTypography centers cleanly on `Public Sans` (48px display down to 16px body), unified by `0.25rem` base corner radius and subtle shadow elevation.\n\nMaintained by **State of New South Wales**. Source: published token package (https://www.digital.nsw.gov.au/digital-design-system), package `nsw-design-system`. Inventory: **91** colors, **24** typography steps, and **35** documented components (ISC license).\n\n### Layout & Spacing\n- **Grid & Control Spacing**: Derived from 35 component tokens with documented paddings: `.125rem 1rem`, `0 1rem`, `.5rem`, `1.5rem 0`, `1rem 1rem 3.875rem`.\n- **Hierarchy**: Group controls cleanly within `#f2f2f2` cards; separate sibling sections using `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` hairlines rather than oversized whitespace.\n\n### Elevation & Depth\n- **Layered Shadow Model**: Uses documented shadows (`0 0.25rem 0.75rem 0 rgba(0,0,0,0.15)`, `0 4px 9px -5px rgba(0,0,0,.4)`) paired with `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` borders for elevated overlays.\n- **Interactive Lift**: Reserve higher surface brightness or focus outlines anchored on `#002664` for keyboard focus and active selection states.",
  "dos": "### Do\n- Anchor base views on `#fff` (light) with `#0b0b0c` primary text and `#0b0b0c` secondary labels.\n- Use `#002664` with `#f7f7f8` text (13.4:1) for primary CTAs, active tabs, and focus outlines.\n- Pair `Public Sans` headings with `Public Sans` body copy using documented weights and scale steps.\n- Apply `0.25rem` base geometry across inputs and buttons (0.25rem on outer containers).\n- Separate containers via `#f2f2f2` surface shifts and `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` hairlines cleanly.\n\n### Don't\n- Do not invert the base canvas out of light polarity without explicitly switching component text tokens.\n- Do not place low-contrast muted ink or raw white text on light accents without verifying >= 4.5:1 WCAG AA contrast.\n- Do not invent arbitrary brand colors, unverified fonts, or synthetic heavy shadows outside the palette above.\n- Do not mix conflicting corner radii that clash with the system's `0.25rem` baseline.\n- Do not truncate or drop border contrast on `input` fields and secondary buttons."
}
